1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,030
Now upon graduating I experienced a different kind of envy.
毕业之后，我经历了另一种嫉妒。

2
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:15,119
I envied people who seemed to have their jobs and careers all figured out and who seemed happy with what they were doing because I did not have that.
我嫉妒那些似乎已经把工作和职业道路想清楚、而且乐在其中的人，因为我当时没有那样的状态。

3
00:00:15,119 --> 00:00:23,829
So I tried to justify my position of dissatisfaction by thinking things like.
所以，我试着用这样一些想法，为自己的不满意状态找理由。

4
00:00:23,839 --> 00:00:32,720
Well the whole reason that they can even live their dreams is because they were luckier or they were better off or they got help.
比如：他们之所以能实现梦想，无非是因为更幸运、条件更好，或者得到了帮助。

5
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:36,880
They had access to things that I did not have access to and whatnot.
他们能接触到我接触不到的资源，诸如此类。

6
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:45,590
And even though there might have been some truth to that it was all just an attempt really to make myself feel better for not having what they had.
即使这些说法可能有几分道理，它们其实也只是为了让我在没拥有那些东西时感觉好一点。

7
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:52,239
By attempting to minimize their accomplishments and this is something that we often do when experiencing envy.
我是通过试图贬低他们的成就来安慰自己；她认为，这也是人在嫉妒时常做的事。

8
00:00:52,239 --> 00:00:57,430
Now did it work did I feel better no of course not.
那么，这样有用吗？我好受了吗？没有，当然没有。

9
00:00:57,440 --> 00:01:06,310
You know at best a victim narrative which is what that was will have you remain stuck.
她认为，这种把自己放在受害者位置的叙事，最好的结果也只是让你继续停滞。

10
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:19,040
But typically it'll actually move you backwards because now not only do you feel dissatisfied with life or career or whatever it might be but you also feel resentful.
但她觉得，这通常还会让你倒退，因为你不只对生活、事业或其他事情不满，还会心怀怨恨。

11
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:23,109
Now here is where we get to the part that I think really is worth reflecting on.
现在我们来到了我觉得真正值得反思的部分。

12
00:01:23,119 --> 00:01:28,000
And it's how I currently deal with any envy that I may experience.
那就是，我现在如何应对自己可能感受到的嫉妒。

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:36,720
So what I ended up realizing was that really envy wasn't about any specific person.
我最终意识到，嫉妒其实并不针对某个特定的人。

14
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:43,920
You know it was only about what they had which in this example was an enjoyable career.
它只是关乎对方拥有的东西；在这个例子里，就是一份令人愉快的事业。

15
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:53,760
And in thinking this way you know in moving the person out of the equation and separating the message from the messenger.
这样思考，把具体那个人从问题中拿开，把信息与传递信息的人分开。

16
00:01:53,760 --> 00:02:00,479
Or the possession or position from the person I was able to do two things.
或者说，把拥有的东西或所处的位置与那个人分开，我就能做到两件事。

17
00:02:00,479 --> 00:02:06,310
So firstly instead of viewing anyone who possessed something that I wanted in a hostile way.
第一，不再以敌对的眼光看待那些拥有我想要之物的人。

18
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:11,200
I started viewing them as people who had enlightened me.
我开始把他们看作让我有所醒悟的人。

19
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:20,790
You know someone who had helped me identify a gap in my life and perhaps even someone that I could set as an example or as a teacher.
也就是，帮助我看见生活中差距的人，甚至可以成为我的榜样或老师的人。

20
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:32,400
And secondly I was able to get more clarity on what exactly it was that I was envying and I could decide what action should follow.
第二，我能更清楚地知道自己究竟在嫉妒什么，并决定接下来该采取什么行动。

21
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:42,080
See in many situations in life there's the option of doing something useful or doing something that isn't useful or perhaps even harmful or doing nothing at all.
你看，生活中的许多情境里，我们可以选择做有用的事，也可以做没用甚至有害的事，或者什么都不做。

22
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:48,630
And how do we choose so I often find myself returning to the serenity prayer.
那该如何选择呢？我常常发现自己会回到《宁静祷文》里的想法。

23
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:58,240
God grant me the serenity to accept the things that I cannot change courage to change the things that I can and wisdom to know the difference.
上帝啊，请赐我宁静，接受不能改变的事；赐我勇气，改变能够改变的事；赐我智慧，辨别两者。

24
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:03,510
Now I already have a video about quitting my job and pursuing what I'm doing now so I won't get into that here.
我已经有一支视频谈过辞职、追求现在所做的事，所以这里就不展开了。

25
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:10,560
But this would be an example of non hostile envy where my envy actually even led me to something good.
但这可以算是没有敌意的嫉妒：我的嫉妒实际上还引导我走向了好事。

26
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:18,310
And now this all begs the question envy always a sign that we lack something we ought to be pursuing.
这也引出了一个问题：嫉妒总是在提示我们，缺少某个应该去追求的东西吗？

27
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:28,230
And is the best thing to do when experiencing envy to seek to improve ourselves or improve our situation.
那么，感到嫉妒时，最好的做法就是努力提升自己或改善处境吗？

28
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:39,350
Well I definitely think that self improvement is the better option as opposed to self destruction or engaging in the destruction of others.
我确实觉得，相比自我毁伤，或者伤害别人，提升自己是更好的选择。

29
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:44,080
But there is also the option of simply doing nothing.
但还有另一个选项，就是单纯什么都不做。

30
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:49,360
You know there may be a lot of things in life that we envy.
生活里可能有许多让我们羡慕、嫉妒的东西。

31
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:55,430
But that doesn't mean that having all of those things would improve our lives or make us happier.
但这并不意味着，拥有所有这些东西，就会让生活更好、让我们更幸福。

32
00:03:55,440 --> 00:04:01,800
Every single emotion that we feel is not a sign that we need to change something.
她认为，并不是我们感受到的每一种情绪，都在提示必须改变什么。

33
00:04:02,479 --> 00:04:09,350
Sometimes we can just let ourselves acknowledge a feeling and then do nothing about it.
有时，我们可以只允许自己承认一种感受，然后不对它采取行动。

34
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:14,080
I like to think of it as seeing a sailboat passing you on a lake.
我喜欢把它想象成，看见一艘帆船从湖面上经过自己身边。

35
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:25,990
And not attempting to throw rocks at it but also not attempting to build your own but simply letting it pass you.
不试图朝它扔石头，也不试图造自己的船，只是让它从身边经过。
